Hydronic HVAC Systems
Utilize piping systems to circulate water and heat throughout a building. Hydronic chilled water systems typically operate in the 40 to 56°F range, while hydronic hot water systems in the 120 to 190°F range. Hydronic condenser water / ambient temperature loop systems are within the 50 to 85°F range.
Natural Gas
The majority of buildings are heated with natural gas, either through forced-air furnaces,
boilers for hydronic systems, radiant floor heating, ductless systems, direct vent
heaters, or district steam produced by burning natural gas. According to Xcel Energy’s
2023 Annual Community Energy Report for the City of Denver, a little more than
225,000 customers use natural gas for all or part of their heating needs1, out of a total
of just over 360,000 total utility customers (approximately 62.5%).
Electricity
Of the remaining 135,000 homes and businesses in Denver, most use electricity as
their primary heating source.


