Today, 110 buildings are served by Xcel Energy District Steam, and 45 customers are served
by District Chilled Water services. The current district energy model in Denver is a dual system
thermal energy network – that is, two completely independent systems. A major drawback of
this model is that in the case of simultaneous heating and cooling, which is a common necessity
